<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Ritual consciousness is more than a preparatory step; it is the foundation upon which the success of any practice is built. By achieving this state, you cultivate a focused and receptive mind, free from distractions, and a body that is calm and balanced. This creates the optimal conditions for the effective application of intent and concentration, which are essential for the success of all subsequent exercises.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (When the body's nervous system is inactive and balanced, it ceases to send signals to the mind, allowing the body to become silent. In this state of physical stillness and mental calm, all external sensory inputs are quieted. What remains is pure awareness, an unclouded state of consciousness that enables deep focus and clarity. With consistent practice, entering ritual consciousness becomes second nature, elevating the quality and effectiveness of every method and technique explored in this guidebook.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
